BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:court-list-01@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261106
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: A petition against deletions in Maharashtra's revisi
 on\, W.P.(C) No. 1330 of 2026. The Court issued notice to the Election Com
 mission on 26 October
DESCRIPTION:A petition against deletions in Maharashtra's revision\, W.P.(C
 ) No. 1330 of 2026. The Court issued notice to the Election Commission on 
 26 October. The petition is listed for hearing. On 26 October the Court de
 clined to extend the time for claims and objections or to stop the final r
 oll before hearing the Commission. Court: Supreme Court. Source: LawChakra
 \, https://lawchakra.in/supreme-court/maharashtra-sir-notice-eci/ More: ht
 tps://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-51
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-46@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:BJP march and public meeting on the SIR in Malappuram
DESCRIPTION:A BJP march in Malappuram followed by a public meeting\, which 
 the party says is part of its nationwide campaign to explain the need for 
 the revision. Organised by Bharatiya Janata Party\, Malappuram (State vice
 -president V. Unnikrishnan inaugurated the planning meeting) (a political 
 party). Place: Malappuram (route and venue not stated). Source: https://ww
 w.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/bjp-to-hold-sir-march-on-november-6/ar
 ticle71623341.ece
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-67@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:'Jantar Mantar at Kochi' march and meeting against the SIR
DESCRIPTION:The actor Prakash Raj led a march from Marine Drive to a meetin
 g at Rajendra Maidan\, where the group's founder\, Abhijeet Dipke\, spoke.
  The protest called for the revision to be withdrawn and the Chief Electio
 n Commissioner to resign. The organisers put the march at about 500\, and 
 the state president of the DYFI\, Chintha Jerome\, took part. Organised by
  Cockroach Janta Party. Place: From Marine Drive to Rajendra Maidan\, Koch
 i. Source: https://www.freepressjournal.in/india/cockroach-janta-party-fou
 nder-abhijeet-dipke-attacks-pm-modi-at-kochi-rally-questions-electoral-rol
 l-revision
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-71@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261113
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Congress village chaupals at which deleted names are to be read out
 \, until 15 December
DESCRIPTION:Village meetings that the Congress has asked its grassroots uni
 ts to hold across the country by 15 December\, at which the names of delet
 ed electors are to be read out. They are part of the party's 'Vote Rakshak
 ' campaign within its 'Vote Bachao\, Desh Bachao' campaign\, under which p
 arty workers are to visit every booth to find deleted electors. K. C. Venu
 gopal announced them after reviewing the campaign on 13 November with the 
 party's state in-charges and state presidents. The party has also opened a
  website\, iamvoterakshak.in\, on which it says people can check whether t
 heir names were deleted\, register a protest and apply to be added again. 
 Organised by Indian National Congress (announced by general secretary (org
 anisation) K. C. Venugopal) (a political party). Place: Villages across th
 e country. Source: https://www.deccanherald.com/india/organise-village-cha
 upals-read-out-deleted-voters-names-congress-tells-grassroots-units-to-int
 ensify-campaign-against-cec-sir-4218499
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-74@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261116
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261117
SUMMARY:Congress 'Vote Bachao\, Desh Bachao' chaupal in Tauru
DESCRIPTION:A village meeting the Congress held in Tauru against the revisi
 on\, under its 'Vote Bachao\, Desh Bachao' campaign. It was attended by th
 e party's Haryana in-charge Sanjay Dutt\, the state president Rao Narender
  Singh\, the AICC observer Rohit Chaudhary\, the Rohtak MLA Bharat Bhushan
  Batra\, who is also the party's Gurgaon district observer\, and the Gurga
 on rural district president Vardhan Yadav. Chaudhary asked party workers t
 o visit households and tell people of their voting rights. The organiser a
 sked that the Election Commission work independently of political interfer
 ence and ensure a free\, fair and transparent election. Organised by India
 n National Congress\, Haryana (organised by a party youth leader and atten
 ded by the state in-charge Sanjay Dutt and the state president Rao Narende
 r Singh) (a political party). Place: Tauru. Source: https://timesofindia.i
 ndiatimes.com/city/gurgaon/cong-holds-sir-protest-with-vote-bachao-campaig
 n/articleshow/135901410.cms
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-77@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261118
SUMMARY:BJP 'Save Democracy\, Eradicate Anarchy' padayatra in Diglipur
DESCRIPTION:A BJP foot march from the party's office in Diglipur to New Dur
 ga Market\, followed by a public meeting near the market\, at which the pa
 rty accused the Congress of politicising the revision. The Andaman Chronic
 le reports that more than 1500 people took part and that the march is part
  of the BJP's campaign across the country to counter the INDIA bloc's narr
 ative against the government at the Centre. Jai Prakash told the meeting t
 hat the Congress had no faith in the SIR process\, and Anil Kumar Tiwari s
 aid the Congress was opposing the revision although voter list revisions h
 ad been carried out several times across the country. Organised by Bharati
 ya Janata Party\, Andaman and Nicobar Islands unit (state president Anil K
 umar Tiwari\, with the party's national secretary and in-charge for the is
 lands\, Jai Prakash) (a political party). Place: From the BJP office in Di
 glipur to New Durga Market\, Diglipur. Source: https://andamanchronicle.ne
 t/diglipur-bjp-holds-save-democracy-padayatra-accuses-cong-of-spreading-li
 es-and-misleading-the-country/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:court-list-03@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261118
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: The petitions alleging that decisions of the Electio
 n Commission\, those on the revision among them\, were taken without the a
 greement of the two Election Commissioners\, led by W.P.(C) No. 1246 of 20
 26
DESCRIPTION:The petitions alleging that decisions of the Election Commissio
 n\, those on the revision among them\, were taken without the agreement of
  the two Election Commissioners\, led by W.P.(C) No. 1246 of 2026. The lea
 d petition is listed for admission as item 26 in the Chief Justice's court
 \, before the Chief Justice\, Justice Joymalya Bagchi and Justice V. Mohan
 a. The court sits from 10:30 am. Seven connected petitions are listed with
  it\, among them the petitions of Asaduddin Owaisi\, of Rahul Gandhi and o
 thers\, of Digvijaya Singh and of Dola Sen. Court: Supreme Court. Source: 
 Supreme Court of India\, daily cause list for 17 November 2026\, https://a
 pi.sci.gov.in/jonew/cl/2026-11-17/M_J_1.pdf More: https://offtheroll.in/in
 dia/disputes/#d-court-53
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:court-list-06@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261120
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: The petition of two transparency activists on Delhi'
 s revision\, W.P.(C) No. 1188 of 2026\, and an application they were told 
 to file on the Commission's letter about Form 6
DESCRIPTION:The petition of two transparency activists on Delhi's revision\
 , W.P.(C) No. 1188 of 2026\, and an application they were told to file on 
 the Commission's letter about Form 6. The petition is listed for admission
  as item 26 in the Chief Justice's court\, before the Chief Justice\, Just
 ice Joymalya Bagchi and Justice V. Mohana\, with an application for clarif
 ication or direction and an intervention application. A connected petition
 \, W.P.(C) No. 1339 of 2026\, is listed with it as item 26.1. The court si
 ts from 10:30 am. On 4 November the Court declined to pass urgent orders a
 nd asked the petitioners to file their application before this date. Court
 : Supreme Court. Source: Supreme Court of India\, daily cause list for 19 
 November 2026\, https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/cl/2026-11-19/M_J_1.pdf More:
  https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-61
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-82@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261122
SUMMARY:Mahila Congress 'Keralam Jantar Mantar' protest at Lok Bhavan\, Thi
 ruvananthapuram
DESCRIPTION:A protest by the Mahila Congress in front of Lok Bhavan in Thir
 uvananthapuram\, demanding the resignation of the Chief Election Commissio
 ner and the withdrawal of the revision. Deepa Dasmunsi inaugurated it and 
 told hundreds of Mahila Congress workers that the Congress would continue 
 its nationwide protests until the Chief Election Commissioner resigned. Je
 bi Mather\, the UDF convenor and MP Adoor Prakash and the Cultural Affairs
  Minister P C Vishnunadh also spoke. The protesters carried effigies of th
 e Chief Election Commissioner. Organised by Mahila Congress\, Kerala unit 
 (state president Jebi Mather)\, inaugurated by the AICC general secretary 
 Deepa Dasmunsi (a political party). Place: In front of Keralam Lok Bhavan\
 , Thiruvananthapuram. Source: https://theprint.in/india/mahila-congress-pr
 otests-in-keralam-demanding-cec-gyanesh-kumars-resignation/3105330/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-80@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:People's Convention on 'SIR and the Challenges to Constitutional De
 mocracy' in Hyderabad
DESCRIPTION:A public convention on the revision that the Forum for Constitu
 tional Democracy announced at a press conference at the Press Club in Bash
 eerbagh on 19 November\, to be addressed by the Supreme Court advocate Pra
 shant Bhushan. The senior advocate G. Jyothy Kiran said it would be the fo
 rum's first public meeting since its formation. At the press conference K.
  Ramachandra Murthy questioned the credibility of elections when the rolls
  themselves are in question\, and Justice B. Sudershan Reddy called the re
 vision arbitrary and questioned its legal and constitutional basis. Justic
 e Reddy alleged that one person had filed Form 7 applications against hund
 reds of voters\, and referred to cases registered in Telangana and Karnata
 ka over such applications. Prof. Kodandaram raised the deletion and altera
 tion of voters' names and said the scale of the revision called for wider 
 public discussion\, and that around 50 intellectuals had come together in 
 the forum. The forum invited citizens\, civil society organisations and de
 mocratic rights activists to attend. Organised by Forum for Constitutional
  Democracy (convenor K. Ramachandra Murthy). Place: Institution of Enginee
 rs (India)\, Khairatabad\, Hyderabad. Source: https://newsmeter.in/hyderab
 ad/hyderabad-sc-lawyer-prashant-bhushan-to-address-convention-on-sir-on-no
 v-22-779662
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-87@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Press conference and vigil of transgender and gender-diverse person
 s on the revision\, Press Club of India
DESCRIPTION:A press conference and community vigil on Transgender Day of Re
 membrance\, at which an alliance of transgender and gender-diverse persons
  pointed to the exclusion of transgender identity cards from the Election 
 Commission's list of 12 accepted documents\, The Tribune reported. On the 
 figures the alliance presented\, registered transgender electors in 12 sta
 tes and union territories fell from 35\,870 to 24\,811 during the revision
 \, a fall of 30.8 per cent and more than 2.5 times the fall in electors ov
 erall. The groups argued that a revision relying heavily on documents held
  by families falls disproportionately on transgender persons estranged fro
 m their families or forced to leave home\, and that changes of name and ad
 dress make it harder for them to show they are eligible. The transparency 
 activist Anjali Bhardwaj said that women and transgender persons often fac
 e hurdles over documents because of changes of name and address and estran
 gement from their families\, and asked whether a change of address should 
 cost a citizen the vote. Organised by An alliance of transgender and gende
 r-diverse persons\, which the report does not name. Place: Press Club of I
 ndia\, New Delhi. Source: https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/delhi/communit
 y-flags-30-8-voter-decline-during-sir-across-12-states/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-81@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261124
SUMMARY:BJP 'Let Us Protect Democracy\, Bury Anarchy' Maha Padayatra in Kar
 imnagar with Nitin Nabin
DESCRIPTION:A BJP rally in Karimnagar to be led by the party's national pre
 sident Nitin Nabin\, which Bandi Sanjay Kumar said on 22 November would co
 unter criticism of the revision and the allegations of vote theft made aga
 inst the party. He said the rally would be historic\, with a massive turno
 ut of BJP activists and people. The Hindu calls it the party's 'Let Us Pro
 tect Democracy\, Bury Anarchy' Maha Padayatra and reports that leaders exp
 ect more than one lakh people to take part. Organised by Bharatiya Janata 
 Party (national president Nitin Nabin\, with the Union Minister of State f
 or Home Affairs and Karimnagar MP Bandi Sanjay Kumar) (a political party).
  Place: Karimnagar. Source: https://www.newindianexpress.com/states/telang
 ana/2026/Nov/22/bjp-president-nitin-nabin-to-lead-rally-against-anti-sir-c
 riticism-in-telangana-on-monday
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:court-list-07@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261124
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: A petition by a group of advocates for guidelines on
  processions and protests near the Supreme Court\, after the Opposition's 
 march of 12 October against the Chief Election Commissioner
DESCRIPTION:A petition by a group of advocates for guidelines on procession
 s and protests near the Supreme Court\, after the Opposition's march of 12
  October against the Chief Election Commissioner. On 3 November the Court 
 sought replies from Mallikarjun Kharge\, Rahul Gandhi and the Centre\, and
  the Centre said it would reply by this date. Court: Supreme Court. Source
 : Hindustan Times\, https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/supreme-cour
 t-rahul-gandhi-mallikarjun-kharge-india-bloc-protest-gyanesh-kumar-1017937
 02344380.html More: https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-62
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-84@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261124
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261125
SUMMARY:Press conference in Mumbai announcing the second phase of the campa
 ign against the revision
DESCRIPTION:A press conference in Mumbai at which activists associated with
  the nationwide protests announced that the second phase of the campaign a
 gainst the revision would begin on Constitution Day\, 26 November\, with a
  focus on Maharashtra and other states where the revision is still incompl
 ete\, the Free Press Journal reported. Representatives of the Association 
 for Protection of Civil Rights\, the People's Union for Civil Liberties\, 
 the Maharashtra SIR Janajagruti Abhiyan and the Cockroach Janta Party call
 ed for the revision to be cancelled and said the Commission had no documen
 ts to show that it had itself taken the decision to conduct it. Anjali Bha
 rdwaj of the National Campaign for People's Right to Information\, the sen
 ior advocate Prashant Bhushan\, Yogendra Yadav of the Bharat Jodo Abhiyan 
 and the advocate Mihir Desai of the PUCL spoke. The paper notes that the S
 upreme Court upheld the Commission's authority to conduct the revision in 
 its judgment of 27 May 2026 on Bihar. Organised by PUCL\, APCR and Maharas
 htra SIR Jagruti Abhiyan\, as the People Against SIR listing gives the hos
 ts. Place: Mumbai. Source: https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-a
 ctivists-to-launch-second-phase-of-anti-sir-campaign-on-constitution-day-d
 emand-cancellation-of-electoral-roll-revision
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-69@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Rally on Anna Salai\, Chennai\, against the SIR
DESCRIPTION:A rally that the collective announced at a press conference at 
 the Chennai Press Club on 10 November\, as part of what it called a nation
 wide day of action against the revision. The political economist Parakala 
 Prabhakar\, the Carnatic vocalist T.M. Krishna\, Thomas Franco\, a former 
 General Secretary of the All India Bank Officers' Confederation\, and the 
 collective's co-convenor Radhika Ganesh spoke at the press conference. The
  collective demanded an inquiry into the fall in Tamil Nadu's roll\, which
  it put at 74.07 lakh names. Prabhakar called for the revision to be scrap
 ped and for every eligible voter whose name was deleted to be restored. Or
 ganised by Independent Young Citizens Collective\, part of People Against 
 SIR. Place: Anna Salai\, Chennai. Source: https://www.thehindu.com/news/na
 tional/tamil-nadu/over-74-lakh-voters-missing-from-tamil-nadu-electoral-ro
 lls-says-citizens-collective/article71685695.ece
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-70@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261221
SUMMARY:Protests across the country called by People Against SIR\, 26 Novem
 ber to 20 December
DESCRIPTION:People Against SIR has called for peaceful protests against the
  revision between 26 November and 20 December\, The Hindu reported. The ca
 ll was decided by the platform's National Coordination Committee and plann
 ed at a meeting of its working group on 12 November. According to the repo
 rt\, the groups would mark Constitution Day on 26 November with demonstrat
 ions across the country to assert the 'Right to Vote\, Right to Livelihood
 '\, and would hold public meetings and rallies and audit voter lists until
  20 December. The agitation would also include dharnas\, a People's Parlia
 ment and a people's referendum. In a statement after the meeting the platf
 orm called the Commission's recent changes belated half measures that leav
 e the mass disenfranchisement unaddressed. The actor Prakash Raj\, who is 
 part of the platform\, spoke to the press\, and the transparency activist 
 Anjali Bhardwaj said the agitation would continue until the revision is sc
 rapped and the Chief Election Commissioner is removed and prosecuted. No p
 lace or date for a single event after 26 November was given. Organised by 
 People Against SIR\, a platform of civil society\, student and farmers' or
 ganisations. Place: Across the country\, beginning with demonstrations on 
 Constitution Day\, 26 November. Source: https://www.thehindu.com/news/nati
 onal/anti-sir-platform-calls-for-mass-agitation-from-november-26-to-decemb
 er-20/article71693775.ece
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-72@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Congress 'Samvidhan Raksha March' by state units on Constitution Da
 y
DESCRIPTION:Marches that the Congress's state units have been tasked to hol
 d on Constitution Day\, 26 November\, as Deccan Herald reported in its acc
 ount of the party's 'Vote Bachao\, Desh Bachao' campaign. The report gives
  them beside the village chaupals that K. C. Venugopal\, the party's gener
 al secretary (organisation)\, announced after reviewing the campaign on 13
  November with the party's state in-charges and state presidents. Organise
 d by Indian National Congress (its state units) (a political party). Place
 : Across the country\, organised by the party's state units. Source: https
 ://www.deccanherald.com/india/organise-village-chaupals-read-out-deleted-v
 oters-names-congress-tells-grassroots-units-to-intensify-campaign-against-
 cec-sir-4218499
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-73@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Uttar Pradesh Congress 'Samvidhan Bachao Sankalp Yatra' on Constitu
 tion Day
DESCRIPTION:A march on Constitution Day from the Congress office to the sta
 tue of B. R. Ambedkar\, which Rajendra Pal Gautam said would raise questio
 ns about the Constitution\, democratic rights and the voter list\, with fo
 ot marches across the state on the same day. Gautam and Aradhana Mishra an
 nounced it at a joint press conference at the party's state headquarters i
 n Lucknow\, with a campaign in which party workers are to check the voter 
 list of every Assembly constituency in the state. At the press conference 
 the two leaders claimed that 15 per cent more women's votes than men's had
  been deleted in the revision. Organised by Indian National Congress\, Utt
 ar Pradesh unit (state in-charge Rajendra Pal Gautam and state president A
 radhana Mishra 'Mona') (a political party). Place: From the Congress offic
 e to the statue of B. R. Ambedkar\, with foot marches across Uttar Pradesh
 . Source: https://www.jagran.com/uttar-pradesh/lucknow-city-congress-to-la
 unch-campaign-to-verify-voter-list-to-launch-rally-on-26th-40437122.html
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-75@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Haryana Congress 'Samvidhan Raksha March' in Panchkula on Constitut
 ion Day
DESCRIPTION:A march in Panchkula on Constitution Day that the Haryana Congr
 ess announced on 17 November\, after a meeting at Jat Bhawan in Karnal of 
 its district presidents\, the state presidents of its wings and other offi
 ce-bearers. Sanjay Dutt said senior party leaders\, MPs\, MLAs\, former ML
 As\, district and block office-bearers\, representatives of frontal organi
 sations and citizens were expected to take part. He said the march is part
  of the party's nationwide initiative under which state units have been as
 ked to organise Constitution Day marches in their states. The party also a
 nnounced a 'Vote Rakshak' drive from 22 to 30 November\, in which Rao Nare
 nder Singh said it would deploy at least one trained volunteer at every po
 lling booth to identify voters whose names have been removed from the roll
 s and verify the circumstances of the deletions. Organised by Indian Natio
 nal Congress\, Haryana unit (state president Rao Narender Singh and the AI
 CC in-charge for Haryana Sanjay Dutt) (a political party). Place: Panchkul
 a. Source: https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/haryana/karnal-congress-to-ro
 ll-out-voter-rights-campaign-plans-constitution-march/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-76@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:BJP rally in Kolkata on Constitution Day to answer the opposition o
 n the revision
DESCRIPTION:A large rally in Kolkata on Constitution Day that the BJP has d
 ecided to hold to answer the opposition's attacks on the revision\, Dainik
  Jagran reported\, with processions in districts across the state. The pap
 er reports that the party aims to reject the opposition's allegation that 
 the Election Commission has been removing electors' names from the rolls a
 t the BJP's behest\, and that the party calls the allegations false. It re
 ports\, citing sources\, that the party is also considering going door to 
 door. Organised by Bharatiya Janata Party\, West Bengal unit (a political 
 party). Place: Kolkata\, with processions in districts across the state. S
 ource: https://www.jagran.com/west-bengal/kolkata-bjp-kolkata-rally-counte
 ring-opposition-on-voter-list-sir-40439668.html
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-78@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Madhya Pradesh Congress 'Samvidhan Raksha March' in Bhopal on Const
 itution Day
DESCRIPTION:A march in Bhopal on Constitution Day that the Congress announc
 ed on 19 November against what it alleges are irregularities in the revisi
 on. Mohammad Arif Naseem Khan\, a special invitee to the Congress Working 
 Committee\, said after a meeting in Indore on the preparations that at lea
 st 1\,000 party workers from each of the state's 230 Assembly constituenci
 es would march to the capital. He alleged that the names of eligible voter
 s are being deleted under the revision at the behest of the BJP. He said t
 he party is also running a 'vote rakshak' campaign in the state\, in which
  its workers go door to door to verify the names of voters who are no long
 er on the rolls. Organised by Indian National Congress\, Madhya Pradesh un
 it (Mohammad Arif Naseem Khan\, a special invitee to the Congress Working 
 Committee\, spoke for it) (a political party). Place: Bhopal. Source: http
 s://theprint.in/india/cong-to-hold-samvidhan-raksha-march-in-bhopal-on-nov
 -26-against-sir-irregularities/3103359/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-85@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Gatherings of 26 November added to the People Against SIR map
DESCRIPTION:Eight gatherings against the revision that the People Against S
 IR map lists for Constitution Day\, 26 November\, in Jharkhand\, Kerala\, 
 Punjab and Haryana. The four in Punjab\, at Amritsar\, Jalandhar\, Patiala
  and Bathinda\, name SKM as host\, and the Thrissur listing names Wake Up 
 Keralam. The Ranchi listing gives Jaipal Singh Munda Stadium at 11:00 am\,
  and the Jamshedpur listing gives 11:00 am with no venue. The Bahadurgarh 
 listing in Haryana gives no venue\, time or host. The alliance says on its
  own site that it will read the Preamble aloud in every city that day. Org
 anised by . Place: Ranchi\, Jamshedpur\, Thrissur\, Amritsar\, Jalandhar\,
  Patiala\, Bathinda and Bahadurgarh. Source: https://peopleagainstsir.org/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-88@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:March from Valmiki Sadan to Jantar Mantar\, New Delhi\, on Constitu
 tion Day
DESCRIPTION:A march against the revision on Constitution Day that the Peopl
 e Against SIR map lists at Mandir Marg\, New Delhi\, at 12:30 pm\, with SK
 M\, AIKS\, AISA\, SFI\, DYFI and Collective as hosts. A senior New Delhi p
 olice officer told The Hindu that no permission had been sought from the D
 elhi Police for the march\, and the organisers have maintained that they i
 nformed the police of it\, the paper reported. The paper's standfirst says
  that People Against SIR\, which it describes as a collective of about 200
  organisations\, has informed the Delhi Police of the march\, from Valmiki
  Sadan to Jantar Mantar. On the night of 25 November the New Delhi police 
 posted a notice saying it had received no application for a march by the S
 KM and other activists from Kali Bari to Jantar Mantar and had granted no 
 permission\, and that prohibitory orders under Section 163 of the Bharatiy
 a Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita were in force in the New Delhi district\, The W
 ire and The Times of India reported. Organised by SKM\, AIKS\, AISA\, SFI\
 , DYFI and Collective\, as the People Against SIR listing gives the hosts.
  Place: Mandir Marg\, New Delhi. Source: https://www.thehindu.com/news/cit
 ies/Delhi/no-permission-sought-for-november-26-anti-sir-march-says-delhi-p
 olice/article71741234.ece
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-89@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Gatherings of 26 November in Uttar Pradesh and Haryana hosted by SK
 M and NSM\, on the People Against SIR map
DESCRIPTION:Nine gatherings against the revision that the People Against SI
 R map lists for Constitution Day\, 26 November\, three in Uttar Pradesh\, 
 at Meerut\, Kanpur and Bareilly\, and six in Haryana\, at Hisar\, Sirsa\, 
 Ambala\, Karnal\, Fatehabad and Kaithal. Every one of them names SKM and N
 SM as hosts. The Meerut listing gives the DM office at 12:20 pm\, and the 
 other eight give no venue or time. Organised by SKM and NSM\, as the listi
 ngs give the hosts. Place: Meerut\, Kanpur and Bareilly in Uttar Pradesh\,
  and Hisar\, Sirsa\, Ambala\, Karnal\, Fatehabad and Kaithal in Haryana. S
 ource: https://peopleagainstsir.org/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-90@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Cockroach Janta Party's 'Save Democracy\, Save Constitution' rally 
 at Samvidhan Chowk\, Nagpur
DESCRIPTION:A 'Save Democracy\, Save Constitution' rally in Nagpur on Const
 itution Day against the Election Commission and the revision\, which Abhij
 eet Dipke of the Cockroach Janta Party announced at a press conference in 
 Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar on 24 November\, ANI reported. The People Agains
 t SIR map lists it at Samvidhan Chowk at 4:00 pm with the group as host. D
 ipke said the group would neither contest the coming state elections direc
 tly nor support any political party\, and he demanded transparent data and
  accountability from the Commission over what he alleged were irregulariti
 es in Maharashtra. Organised by Cockroach Janta Party (announced by Abhije
 et Dipke). Place: Samvidhan Chowk\, Nagpur. Source: https://www.freepressj
 ournal.in/india/chalo-nagpur-abhijeet-dipke-announces-save-democracy-save-
 constitution-rally-against-ecis-sir-exercise-on-november-26
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-91@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Gathering at Gandhi Murti\, Gandhi Maidan\, Patna
DESCRIPTION:A gathering against the revision on Constitution Day\, listed o
 n the People Against SIR map. Organised by Hum Bharat Ke Log. Place: Gandh
 i Murti\, Gandhi Maidan\, Patna. Source: https://peopleagainstsir.org/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-92@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Gathering at Shaheed Smarak\, Gol Bazaar\, Jabalpur
DESCRIPTION:A gathering against the revision on Constitution Day\, listed o
 n the People Against SIR map. Organised by . Place: Shaheed Smarak\, Gol B
 azaar\, Jabalpur. Source: https://peopleagainstsir.org/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-93@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Andhra Pradesh Congress 'Samvidhan Raksha March' in Vijayawada on C
 onstitution Day
DESCRIPTION:A state-level 'Samvidhan Raksha March' on Constitution Day from
  Andhra Ratna Bhavan in Vijayawada at 11:00 am to the statue of B. R. Ambe
 dkar at the PWD Grounds\, which Kolanukonda Sivaji\, vice president of the
  Andhra Pradesh Congress Committee\, announced on 21 November\, PTI report
 ed. He said the party would hold Constitution protection marches across th
 e state that day\, and he asked party leaders and workers\, people's organ
 isations and civil society groups to take part. Organised by Indian Nation
 al Congress\, Andhra Pradesh unit (announced by Kolanukonda Sivaji\, vice 
 president of the Andhra Pradesh Congress Committee) (a political party). P
 lace: From Andhra Ratna Bhavan to the statue of B. R. Ambedkar at the PWD 
 Grounds\, Vijayawada. Source: https://theprint.in/india/cong-to-undertake-
 constitution-protection-marches-on-nov-26-across-andhra/3105327/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-94@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Gathering at Veli Ground\, Fort Kochi
DESCRIPTION:A gathering against the revision on Constitution Day\, listed o
 n the People Against SIR map. Organised by People's Collective Kochi. Plac
 e: Veli Ground\, Fort Kochi. Source: https://peopleagainstsir.org/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-95@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Gatherings of 26 November hosted by SFI\, on the People Against SIR
  map
DESCRIPTION:Twenty-two gatherings against the revision that the People Agai
 nst SIR map lists for Constitution Day\, 26 November\, in 21 places across
  15 states and Puducherry\, each naming SFI as host and giving a venue and
  a time. In Andhra Pradesh they are at the Ambedkar Statue in Vijayawada a
 t 8:00 am\, Ambedkar Junction in Vizianagaram at 10:00 am and the Clock To
 wer in Anantapur at 10:00 am. In West Bengal they are on College Street in
  Kolkata and at the Lenin Statue in Jadavpur\, both at 3:00 pm. In Haryana
  they are at MDU in Rohtak at 2:30 pm and at the Rani Talab protest site i
 n Jind at 11:00 am\, and in Madhya Pradesh at Prabhat Chauraha in Bhopal a
 t 3:00 pm and Phoolbag Chauraha in Gwalior at 2:00 pm. Sambhaji Nagar has 
 two\, at the Bhagat Singh School at 9:00 am and at BAMU at 7:00 pm. The ot
 hers are at Nehru Park in Guwahati at 12:00 pm\, Narol in Ahmedabad at 6:3
 0 pm\, a rally on Mall Road in Shimla at 3:00 pm\, Freedom Park in Bengalu
 ru at 3:30 pm\, Palayam in Thiruvananthapuram at 10:30 am\, Balagandi Bhak
 ta Salabega Pitha in Puri at 4:00 pm\, Swadeshi Mill Junction in Puducherr
 y at 10:00 am\, Ambedkar Manimandapam in Adyar\, Chennai\, at 2:00 pm\, Na
 rayanaguda and Himayathnagar in Hyderabad at 11:30 am\, Parivartan Chowk i
 n Lucknow at 2:00 pm and Gandhi Park in Dehradun at 5:00 pm. Organised by 
 SFI\, as the listings give the host. Place: Vijayawada\, Vizianagaram\, An
 antapur\, Guwahati\, Ahmedabad\, Rohtak\, Jind\, Shimla\, Bengaluru\, Thir
 uvananthapuram\, Bhopal\, Gwalior\, Sambhaji Nagar\, Puri\, Puducherry\, C
 hennai\, Hyderabad\, Lucknow\, Dehradun\, Kolkata and Jadavpur. Source: ht
 tps://peopleagainstsir.org/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
