SUMMARY:Supreme Court (listed tentatively): The petitions on the restrictio
 ns imposed during the protests against the Chief Election Commissioner in 
 October\, led by MA Baby v
DESCRIPTION:The petitions on the restrictions imposed during the protests a
 gainst the Chief Election Commissioner in October\, led by MA Baby v. Unio
 n of India\, with which the Court will hear the petition of two traders' a
 ssociations on their business losses and on Ramlila Maidan as a protest si
 te\, W.P.(C) No. 1395 of 2026. The petitions are tentatively listed for he
 aring. On 18 November the Court issued notice on the traders' petition to 
 the Cockroach Janta Party\, the Congress\, the Aam Aadmi Party and the All
  India Students' Association\, and said it would be heard with these petit
 ions. The court listed the matter for this date tentatively. Court: Suprem
 e Court. Source: LiveLaw\, https://www.livelaw.in/top-stories/supreme-cour
 t-issues-notice-to-cjp-congress-aap-aisa-on-delhi-traders-plea-against-pro
 tests-558913 More: https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-88
