SUMMARY:Supreme Court: The West Bengal government's appeal against the Calc
 utta High Court division bench's order restraining the State Election Comm
 ission from notifying the Kolkata Municipal Corporation elections until th
 e challenge to the delimitation of the wards is decided\, The State of Wes
 t Bengal and another v
DESCRIPTION:The West Bengal government's appeal against the Calcutta High C
 ourt division bench's order restraining the State Election Commission from
  notifying the Kolkata Municipal Corporation elections until the challenge
  to the delimitation of the wards is decided\, The State of West Bengal an
 d another v. Dipu Das and others. On 25 November the Court said it was inc
 lined to stay the High Court's order and to have the challenge transferred
  to the High Court's division bench\, and asked the Solicitor General to s
 eek instructions by this date. Court: Supreme Court. Source: ThePrint (PTI
 )\, https://theprint.in/india/sc-inclined-to-stay-calcutta-hc-order-deferr
 ing-civic-polls-till-decision-on-ward-delimitation/3108337/ More: https://
