SUMMARY:Supreme Court: The petitions alleging that decisions of the Electio
 n Commission\, those on the revision among them\, were taken without the a
 greement of the two Election Commissioners\, led by W.P.(C) No. 1246 of 20
 26\, with the application by Rahul Gandhi and ten other opposition leaders
  to put 48 written questions to the Commission
DESCRIPTION:The petitions alleging that decisions of the Election Commissio
 n\, those on the revision among them\, were taken without the agreement of
  the two Election Commissioners\, led by W.P.(C) No. 1246 of 2026\, with t
 he application by Rahul Gandhi and ten other opposition leaders to put 48 
 written questions to the Commission. The petitions are listed for hearing.
  On 17 November the Court said it would hear the matter after the Election
  Commission files its objections to the application for the 48 questions. 
 Court: Supreme Court. Source: Bar and Bench\, https://www.barandbench.com/
 news/rahul-gandhis-plea-to-serve-48-interrogatories-on-eci-supreme-court-t
 o-decide-after-considering-ecis-objections More: https://offtheroll.in/ind
