UID:ev-79@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261212
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261213
SUMMARY:INDIA bloc rally in Bhopal against the revision
DESCRIPTION:A large rally of the INDIA bloc proposed for Bhopal on 12 Decem
 ber\, against what the parties allege are irregularities in the revision\,
  Dainik Jagran reported. The paper reports that a meeting in Delhi on 19 N
 ovember decided to take the agitation from Delhi to the capitals of the st
 ates\, beginning with Bhopal\, and to hold a 'vote rakshak' march as well.
  It reports that the Congress president Mallikarjun Kharge\, the Leader of
  the Opposition in the Lok Sabha Rahul Gandhi\, the MP Priyanka Gandhi Vad
 ra and the Samajwadi Party president Akhilesh Yadav are to attend with sen
 ior leaders of other parties. Jitu Patwari confirmed the rally and said le
 aders of all the alliance's parties would take part and that more than one
  lakh people would gather. Organised by The INDIA bloc of opposition parti
 es (the Madhya Pradesh Congress president Jitu Patwari confirmed it) (a po
 litical party). Place: Bhopal. Source: https://www.jagran.com/madhya-prade
 sh/bhopal-indi-alliance-bhopal-rally-rahul-priyanka-akhilesh-to-attend-404
 42202.html
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:court-list-08@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261219
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: Petitions by the RJD Member of Parliament Manoj Jha 
 and an advocate challenging section 16 of the Act of 2023 on the Chief Ele
 ction Commissioner and the Election Commissioners\, which bars civil and c
 riminal proceedings against them for their official acts
DESCRIPTION:Petitions by the RJD Member of Parliament Manoj Jha and an advo
 cate challenging section 16 of the Act of 2023 on the Chief Election Commi
 ssioner and the Election Commissioners\, which bars civil and criminal pro
 ceedings against them for their official acts. The Court issued notice to 
 the Centre and the Election Commission on 4 November. The petitions are li
 sted for hearing. Court: Supreme Court. Source: The Hindu\, https://www.th
 ehindu.com/news/national/sc-seeks-centre-ec-response-on-law-giving-blanket
 -lifelong-immunity-to-cec-election-commissioners/article71664699.ece More:
  https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-64
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
